Hi Claudine,

I've added you to the google group.

I've never seen that error before.  It suggests either:

(a) you have some very old version of R
(b) you have some new combination of R / operating system that breaks something that has been working for everyone else.

I would:

1. Upgrade to the newest R, re-install the packages, and see if the error happens using the example script
2. If that doesn't work, download a version of R from a few months ago and try that.

Report back either way!

Cheers, Nick

